Falsifies `designware_mobile_storage::proofs::a_served_block_never_leaves_its_window`.

The defect: the window's bound is off by one block, so a request for the block just past the
window is translated. On radon that block is the first sectors after nife's window: another
partition's, or the boot partition's.

Expected to fail: `assert!(lba + span <= w.first + w.sectors)`, on any request ending one block past
the window.

diff --git a/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/serve.rs b/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/serve.rs
--- a/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/serve.rs
+++ b/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/serve.rs
@@ -56,7 +56,7 @@
         let Some(end) = block.checked_add(count) else {
             return None;
         };
-        if count == 0 || end > self.blocks() {
+        if count == 0 || end > self.blocks() + 1 {
             return None;
         }
         // `block * SECTORS_PER_BLOCK` is at most `sectors` here; the sum is checked so a window
